# 1. Ignore everything by default to prevent folder soup
*

# 2. Allow Git to traverse directories
!*/

# 3. Track specific Root Files
!.gitignore
!main.py
!config_manager.py
!requirements.txt
!README.md

# =======================================================
# 4. TRACK ENTIRE CODE FOLDERS (BEST PRACTICE)
# The /** tells Git to track all files and subfolders inside
# =======================================================
!core/**
!gui/**
!utils/**
!scripts/**

# =======================================================
# 5. RE-IGNORE GENERATED JUNK INSIDE TRACKED FOLDERS
# Even though we track the folders above, we still want
# to ignore Python's auto-generated cache files inside them.
# =======================================================
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.log
.env